<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="e2ddf479">&lt;p&gt;
    Transition design planning should address:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Planning and coordination of resources so that the requirements in the service management strategy and plan are
        effectively realized.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Identification, management and control the risks of failure and disruption across transition activities.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Assurance that all parties adopt the common framework of standard re-usable processes and supporting systems.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Provision of clear and comprehensive plans that enable the customer and business change projects to align their
        activities with the service management plan.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Management of all necessary work-arounds and temporary interfaces.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    The transitional design plan is a living document until the final version is signed off. New inputs, constraints and
    business requirements will drive periodic updates to the transitional design plan.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="f2d680be"></attribute>
<attribute name="usageGuidance" nodeId="a35eae69"></attribute>
<attribute name="refinedDescription" nodeId="ef838b55">&lt;p&gt;
    The transitional design plan provides an integrated approach to transition planning. It improves alignment of service
    management cutover and deployment plans, and helps to:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Plan appropriate capacity and resources for transitional states, and process flows including all necessary
        work-arounds and temporary interfaces.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Provide support for the service transition teams and people.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Plan the changes required in a manner that maintains the integrity of all identified customer assets, service
        assets and configurations&amp;nbsp;as they evolve through service transition.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Verify&amp;nbsp;that service transition issues, risks and deviations are reported to the appropriate stakeholders and
        decision makers.&lt;br /&gt;
        Coordinate activities across projects, suppliers and service teams where required.
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Periodically update the transitional design plan to account for changes that affect cutover planning, to verify
        that the plan is up-to-date and reflects the latest state of the implementation.
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
</Element>
